Every effect, the animation engine, and the rendering are ttfx's — which is
itself a byte-exact Rust port of ChrisBuilds' TerminalTextEffects. ttfx is
consumed here as an unmodified dependency, pinned to a release tag; it is not
forked and not vendored. Because the engine is statically linked into the
built bundle, both copyrights above travel with any binary distributed from
this project, and both appear in LICENSE.

What this project adds is the macOS side: a ScreenSaverView that renders the
engine's frames with CoreText, an SGR interpreter, the configure sheet, and
the bundle build. None of the art originates here.

The screensaver's behavior — canvas filling the screen, logo centered, a
random effect each cycle — is modeled on Omarchy's screensaver
(https://github.com/basecamp/omarchy, bin/omarchy-cmd-screensaver). That is a
design credit, not a code one: no Omarchy code is included, only the same
choice of engine parameters.

